---
import { cta, site } from '../../lib/site';
---

<section id="book" class="relative container-page py-section">
	<!-- No reveal here: by the conversion section the page should be still
	     and certain — and the CTA below renders instantly regardless. -->
	<div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[7fr_5fr] lg:gap-16">
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<p class="eyebrow">From the chef</p>
			<h2 class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">Bring one real menu or order.</h2>
			<p class="mt-7 max-w-[58ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
				I spent twelve years cooking professionally before becoming a software engineer.
				CostCook is the system I wanted when one menu had to become a quote, shopping list,
				prep plan, and pack list without losing the cost along the way.
			</p>
			<div class="mt-5 flex items-center gap-4">
				<img
					src="/founder.jpg"
					alt={`${site.founderName}, the chef who built CostCook`}
					width="384"
					height="384"
					loading="lazy"
					class="w-20 shrink-0 -rotate-[1.5deg] bg-paper p-1 shadow-ticket"
				/>
				<p class="font-display text-xl font-medium">{site.founderName}</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="border-t border-hairline-strong pt-6 lg:mt-3">
			<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">A 15-minute working session</h3>
			<p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">
				We&rsquo;ll place your menu or order in CostCook&rsquo;s costing chain and see whether the
				workflow fits your kitchen. CostCook is still early, so this is a practical fit check,
				not a generic sales deck.
			</p>
			<a
				href={cta.href}
				target={cta.target}
				rel={cta.rel}
				aria-label={cta.ariaLabel}
				class="btn-primary mt-7"
			>
				{cta.label}
			</a>
			<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
				Prefer to talk or text? <a href={site.phoneHref} class="font-medium text-green-deep underline decoration-current underline-offset-4">{site.phone}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
